<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>About &amp; sourcing policy — {{ brand.PUBLICATION }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="How {{ brand.PUBLICATION }} selects sources, credits them, and handles removal requests.">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ brand.SITE_URL }}/about.html">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ brand.SITE_NAME }}">
<meta property="og:title" content="About &amp; sourcing policy — {{ brand.PUBLICATION }}">
<meta property="og:description" content="How {{ brand.PUBLICATION }} selects sources, credits them, and handles removal requests.">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ brand.SITE_URL }}/about.html">
<style>
  /* The same ground, ink and measure as an issue and the archive. This page
     used to be hand-written and had drifted into its own palette, its own font
     stack and a dark-mode block no other page has — which is how it also ended
     up still calling the publication by its old name. Single-theme by choice;
     there is deliberately no dark variant. */
  :root {
    --page: #ffffff; --ink: #16191d; --ink-soft: #545e69; --ink-faint: #8b959f;
    --rule: #e4e8eb; --link: #0b5fbe;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; background: var(--page); color: var(--ink);
    font: 15px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.25rem 1.15rem 4rem; }

  h1.wordmark { margin: 0; font-size: 0; line-height: 0; }
  h1.wordmark img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; }
  .fallback {
    border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem 1.4rem 1.6rem; color: #fff;
    background: linear-gradient(155deg, #3585b8 0%, #1d5f92 45%, #102a3f 100%);
  }
  .fallback .name { margin: 0; font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.035em; }

  .dateline {
    margin: .8rem 0 0; font-size: .79rem; color: var(--ink-faint);
    padding-bottom: .7rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .dateline a { color: var(--link); }

  h2.title {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 .2rem; font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -.02em;
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 2rem 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.02rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -.015em;
  }
  p { margin: .7rem 0; text-wrap: pretty; }
  a { color: var(--link); }
  ul { margin: .6rem 0; padding-left: 1.15rem; }
  li { margin: .35rem 0; }
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: .88em; background: #f4f6f8; padding: .08em .3em; border-radius: 3px;
  }

  footer {
    margin-top: 2.6rem; padding-top: 1.1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: .82rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  footer a { color: var(--link); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <header>
    {% if header %}
    <h1 class="wordmark">
      <a href="./"><img src="{{ header[0] }}"
        {%- if header[1] %} width="{{ header[1] }}"{% endif %}
        {%- if header[2] %} height="{{ header[2] }}"{% endif %}
        alt="{{ brand.PUBLICATION }} — {{ brand.SITE_NAME }}. {{ brand.TAGLINE }}"></a>
    </h1>
    {% else %}
    <div class="fallback"><p class="name">{{ brand.PUBLICATION }}</p></div>
    {% endif %}
    <p class="dateline"><a href="./">← the current issue</a></p>
  </header>

  <h2 class="title">About &amp; sourcing policy</h2>

  {# Publication name and cadence come from brand.py, never typed. The previous
     hand-written version of this page said "Daily Dive" and "each morning" for
     weeks after the rename, because nothing tied the words to the source of
     truth. #}
  <p>
    <strong>{{ brand.SITE_NAME }}'s {{ brand.PUBLICATION }}</strong> is a
    {{ brand.CADENCE }} digest of saltwater and reef aquarium news across
    industry and product announcements, husbandry and science, notable forum
    discussion, new videos, livestock and coral news, wild reef conditions, and
    club events.
  </p>

  <p>
    It is assembled automatically each {{ brand.CADENCE_NOUN }} and
    reviewed and edited by one person — me, {{ brand.EDITOR }}. This is a
    personal project, but also a shared publication for those interested in the
    deeper side of the reef aquarium hobby and industry. I am not affiliated
    with any of the outlets it links to.
  </p>

  <h3>How sources are selected</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Only outlets that publish a public feed or API. Nothing here is scraped.</li>
    <li>Sources are chosen for signal, not completeness. This is a digest, not an archive.</li>
    <li>Anything that reads as an ad rather than news is filtered out.</li>
    <li>A few items each issue are added by hand — stories worth reading that no
        feed here carries. They are credited to the site that published them, on
        the same terms as everything else.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How sources are credited</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Every item names its outlet and links to the original. That link is the point.</li>
    <li>Summaries are short and in my own words — facts and context, never a replacement
        for reading the source.</li>
    <li>No article text is reproduced. Quotes, where they appear, are brief and attributed.</li>
    <li>Every issue lists all the outlets it drew from.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How the crawler behaves</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Honors <code>robots.txt</code> on every request.</li>
    {# DailyDiveBot is deliberately NOT renamed alongside the publication:
       publishers may have allowlisted the string, and changing it would make us
       an unrecognised agent overnight. Leave it. #}
    <li>Identifies itself as <code>{{ brand.BOT_NAME }}</code> with a working contact address.</li>
    <li>No more than one request per second per site.</li>
    <li>Uses conditional requests, so an unchanged feed costs the host almost nothing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Corrections and removal</h3>
  <p>
    If you publish something that appears here and you'd like it removed, your feed
    excluded, or a credit corrected, email
    <a href="mailto:{{ brand.CONTACT_EMAIL }}">{{ brand.CONTACT_EMAIL }}</a>.
    No justification needed — I'll remove it and it stays removed.
  </p>

  <footer>
    <p>
      <a href="./">Current issue</a> · <a href="archive.html">Back issues</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <em>{{ brand.PUBLICATION }}</em> is an automated digest that links to
      reporting it does not own. Every item credits and links its source.
    </p>
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
